---
title: Drunkard’s walk
---
A digger staggers at random through solid rock, and more follow until enough of the map is open [[t:87-97 s:11]].

## The rule
```text
start solid; the first digger starts at the center
a digger steps in a random direction and digs where it lands,
    until it leaves the map or runs out of steps
while less than a share of the map is open:
    start another digger on a random open tile
```

The talk has each new digger spawn somewhere within the open map, and stops when a third of the map is open [[t:95-97]].

## Step through it
@@steps limit=5 mid=1

## Controls
@@control lifetime
How many steps a digger takes. The demo stops a digger once its step count is over 200 [[c04:71-74]].
@@control floor_divisor
Diggers keep coming until one over this number of the map’s tiles is open: a third, in the demo [[c04:25 t:97]].

## What it produces, measured
@@measured

The talk says this map is guaranteed to be contiguous [[t:99-100]]. It is {{c04.regions.max}} region on every seed here [[run:c04.regions.max]]. Its passages are wide: a corridor ratio of {{c04.corridor_ratio.median}} at the median, against cellular automata’s {{c03.corridor_ratio.median}} [[run:c04.corridor_ratio.median c03.corridor_ratio.median]].

## Where it fails
@@fails

The demo’s loop of diggers has no cap but the open share it waits for [[c04:25]].

## What it combines with
@@combines

The talk suggests it for limestone caverns [[t:100-102]].

